# Advisor markdown

`local/advisor/YYYY-MM-DD-ADVISOR-<title>.md` is the local developer's note, for example `2026-11-05-ADVISOR-example.md`. It is shorter than the paired XML of the same name in `audit/advisor/`.

- Write the body in the brief's language. Keep both HTML comments exactly as written.
- Put work the agent cannot do under `<!-- advisor:developer-steps -->`, as unchecked `- [ ]` items.
- Those checkboxes are the `/advisor --execute` gate. Agents do not tick them.
- Do not copy XML rationale, rejected alternatives, or evidence lists into this file.

```markdown
## Developer steps
<!-- advisor:developer-steps -->

- [ ] Create the API key and store it outside git.
```

`None.` under the marker means there is no human step.
